1
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:04,482
They say the firstborn has to set the example.

2
00:00:04,532 --> 00:00:06,087
Has to be more mature.

3
00:00:06,137 --> 00:00:07,651
Has to understand more.

4
00:00:07,701 --> 00:00:09,610
Has to be someone others can rely on.

5
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:12,987
But no one ever asked

6
00:00:13,037 --> 00:00:15,440
if we were ready to be all of that.

7
00:00:19,700 --> 00:00:21,256
We were just born first.

8
00:00:21,306 --> 00:00:22,958
Then, somewhere along the way,

9
00:00:23,008 --> 00:00:26,320
that became the reason we were always expected to give more.

10
00:00:30,700 --> 00:00:32,865
We learned to hold back what we wanted.

11
00:00:32,915 --> 00:00:34,649
Learned to say "it's okay,"

12
00:00:34,699 --> 00:00:37,620
even when everything felt too heavy.

13
00:00:41,700 --> 00:00:43,763
Because there were younger siblings to think about.

14
00:00:43,813 --> 00:00:46,495
Parents we didn't want to disappoint.

15
00:00:46,545 --> 00:00:50,110
Circumstances that made us look like we were fine.

16
00:00:53,900 --> 00:00:56,418
And maybe the most exhausting part

17
00:00:56,468 --> 00:00:59,570
of being the firstborn isn't the responsibility.

18
00:01:04,900 --> 00:01:08,630
It's the guilt every time we want to choose ourselves.

19
00:01:14,200 --> 00:01:17,242
As if resting were a kind of selfishness.

20
00:01:17,292 --> 00:01:21,240
As if failing were something we weren't allowed to do.

21
00:01:25,400 --> 00:01:28,196
When really, this is our first time living, too.

22
00:01:28,246 --> 00:01:30,920
We don't always know what to do either.

23
00:01:34,900 --> 00:01:38,188
And sometimes, the one

24
00:01:38,238 --> 00:01:40,720
everyone leans on needs someone to lean on, too.

25
00:01:45,800 --> 00:01:47,755
So, you're allowed to be tired.

26
00:01:47,805 --> 00:01:49,550
You're allowed to feel lost.

27
00:01:49,600 --> 00:01:51,378
You're allowed to have dreams that have

28
00:01:51,428 --> 00:01:53,603
nothing to do with anyone's expectations.

29
00:01:53,653 --> 00:01:56,630
Because your life is yours to live, too.

30
00:01:59,300 --> 00:02:02,768
Before being the older sibling, before being the family's pride,

31
00:02:02,818 --> 00:02:05,895
before being the one everyone relies on...

32
00:02:05,945 --> 00:02:07,910
you were a child, too.

33
00:02:10,800 --> 00:02:18,500
You were their first child.
Not their second parent.

